  "premise_review": [
    "The entire source FixedTensor structure and both exact theorems form one coherent component. Preserve C/F/nabla/e/X and every dependent field: tensor : TensorSection F X, horizontal : nabla.horizontal X tensor.underlyingSection and fixed : e.map X tensor.underlyingSection = tensor.underlyingSection. There is no independently selected bare proposition field in this local structure.",
    "The fixed field is an actual equality of sections under the supplied pointwise endomorphism; horizontal is an application of the predicate already supplied by nabla. The exact Connection provider chooses that predicate independently of Nabla, flat or integrable, so no differential-kernel definition of horizontality or analytic flatness theorem is inferred.",
    "The complete TensorSection provider was read as context: it supplies rank, carrier, value and underlyingSection independently. No relation between the carrier/value and the underlying section, tensor product construction or algebraic tensor identity is encoded. The copied FixedTensor uses precisely its underlyingSection.",
    "The exact CrystalEndomorphism provider is an arbitrary dependent family of maps F.Section X -> F.Section X with a label. FixedTensor assumes no HeatCompatibleEndomorphism, heat flow, naturality or restriction compatibility proof; importing the provider does not add those premises.",
    "fixed_tensor_is_horizontal and fixed_tensor_is_fixed are genuine proofs obtained by T.horizontal and T.fixed, respectively. They retain all full original C/F/nabla/e/X/T parameters and establish only properties already required by supplied T; they do not construct any fixed section or prove existence or uniqueness.",
    "The exact source imports remain unchanged. Only outer containing namespaces are rebound; explicit open Folder/open Folder.CrystallineTensor restore intended lookup of the original provider types. The same local FixedTensor record and its complete proofs stay together, without a new legacy self-provider import, type narrowing, new alias or provider substitution.",
    "No crystalline cohomology, tensor-product realization, differential equation, heat compatibility, analytic fixed-point, BinaryMatrix or arithmetic consequence is proved by this component. Historical import/namespace elaboration remains unresolved and no Lean replay or mathematical admission is asserted."
  ],
